 {:seon.task/name "the-daily-full-run-is-a-service-run"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner: Optimization (seon.fx). The daily full run (seon.prove full-request, :full mode) is a :tests effect that runs bin/test --all in a worktree of main (fx.clj, the full run's body): its own plan and shards, outside the service's admission. Plan: the full run is a request of the service like any other, its items every test and step of main at its digest with reuse off (:fresh? true items), so one admission covers it and its verdicts land as any run's do; seon.prove/full-answered's red-as-problem stays. Then the full run's shell body has no caller (seon.prove/the-shell-runner-is-deleted). Proof to write: a :full request's items are every key of main, none reused."
